<title>UK: UK's BBA looking to sell division - paper.</title>
<headline>UK's BBA looking to sell division - paper.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>British-based engineering and materials firm BBA Group Plc is set to put its specialist electrical division up for sale, said the Sunday Telegraph newspaper.</p>
<p>It said that the disposal, which would include the business of Haefly Trench, could fetch up to 250 million pounds ($421.4 million) and would be used for acquisitions as well as expanding the company's three remaining divisions - non-woven textiles, flight services and frictions materials.</p>
<p>-London Newsroom +44 171 542 4019</p>
<p>($ = 0.593 British Pounds)</p>
